<title>FRANCE: Castorama 1996 net profit up 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Castorama 1996 net profit up 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable, pre exceptional    553  vs     544</p>
<p>    Net, pre-exceptional		     554  vs     546</p>
<p>    Net attributable per share (francs)  34.90 vs  34.80</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		    11.00 vs  11.00</p>
<p>    Turnover				     17,916 vs 16,410</p>
<p>NOTE - Groupe Castorama gave its results in a statement. It said it had invested 900 million francs in 1996 and had a budget of one billion francs for expansion in 1997.</p>
<p>It also said it would proceed with its plan to buy 100 percent of Canadian retailer Reno-Depot Inc. in line with its January 27 offer. It said Reno-Depot had sales of C$431.5 million in 1996 excluding taxes.</p>
<p>((-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452))</p>
